  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p><b>Send events to an SNS topic, then subscribe each SQS queue to the topic and configure a filter policy for each subscription</b> is the best approach.<br><br>AWS SNS supports native integration with SQS, meaning each queue can independently subscribe to the SNS topic and receive a copy of every event. What's more, SNS subscription filter policies allow you to specify which events each queue receives—solving the requirement to deliver only relevant subsets to each downstream pipeline, and doing so without custom code.<br><br><i>Write events to an SNS topic, subscribe each SQS queue, and use a Lambda function in each pipeline to poll and filter events from its queue</i> is less efficient. Each SQS queue would receive all events, even the irrelevant ones, leading to unnecessary message processing and potential cost/waste.<br><br><i>Deliver events directly to an SQS queue, have a Lambda function extract, filter, and forward events to multiple SQS queues as needed</i> introduces additional Lambda invocation and forwarding complexity, increasing latency, cost, and operational burden. It doesn't leverage AWS-native filtering available through SNS.<br><br><i>Use EventBridge as the event bus, have a Lambda pull, filter, and distribute messages to different SQS queues in parallel</i> is more complex and typically unnecessary for straightforward fan-out and filtering to SQS queues. EventBridge is great for complex routing patterns, but SNS with subscription filters is simpler and better suited to this scenario.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Use SNS subscription filter policies to route messages efficiently to only those SQS queues that need them—no Lambda code required.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your team is building an event-driven application.<br>The frontend collects customer requests and sends events to an AWS service.<br>This AWS service must route events to multiple SQS queues at the same time.<br>Each downstream application (event archival, search, replay, etc.) uses its own queue and only requires a filtered subset of events.<br>What's the simplest way to architect this AWS setup to deliver only relevant events to each queue?</p>",
